title: 'a-clock: chrono tabs, concurrency queue, and a real installed app with wake-from-sleep'
summary: Third feature batch plus the shift from dev-server to a real installed app. Added Stopwatch (laps), Timer (presets/custom, beep+notify on completion), and Pomodoro (cycles, ring, chime+notify, editable settings) as background-running tabs. Fixed the ringing overlay so the media sizes by available height and the Dismiss/Snooze buttons are always in frame. Added a distinct wrong-answer buzzer to the puzzle gate. Reworked concurrent alarms into a queue so a second alarm never overwrites the active one (or resets an in-progress puzzle) and never fires side effects prematurely. Built and installed a standalone a-clock.app to /Applications with a login item, and added opt-in macOS wake-from-sleep via a pmset-based Tauri command so alarms fire even when the Mac is asleep.
